WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.902
-My first guest is one of my
all-time favorites.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.704
He's the funniest human.
He's so talented.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.739
I love the guy.
He stars --

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:09.975
stars in and co-wrote
the new movie "Hubie Halloween,"

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:12.711
which premieres
October 7th on Netflix.

00:00:12.711 --> 00:00:15.080
It is awesome, it is funny,
it is scary.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.450
Here is Adam Sandler.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.853
-Yes, Jimmy. Yes, yes.
-This is what I'm talking about.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.120
-Jimmy.
-This is what --

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.089
-You look good.
You look handsome.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.757
-Thank --
Thank you very much.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.125
I appreciate that.
You look good, too.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.760
You got the beard going.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.063
-Yes. Just covering a lot of --
lot of chins.

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:32.665
Lot of chins came in.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.233
-Yeah.
Had to really --

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:37.336
had to really grow this one long
to block those suckers.

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:39.372
-Thank you for being on the show
again, Zooming.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.908
You were on, helped me out when
we were first starting out,

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:44.110
and I appreciate that.
-Yes.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:48.181
-Are you getting used to Zoom?
-Zoom is --

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:52.719
I don't love Zooming as much as
everyone else 'cause the --

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:55.121
It's hard to hang up
on Zoom because people --

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.057
I'm good at hanging up on the --
on a cellphone.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:01.593
You know, pretending I got into
a car accident or something

00:01:01.593 --> 00:01:03.296
and just pressing end.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.464
But Zoom, you got to literally
look at somebody and go,

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.199
"I -- I've had enough of this."

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:09.468
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:10.703
-"This is too much, man.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.171
I don't want
to be around you anymore."

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:14.907
-Yeah.
"Our conversation's over."

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:18.511
And you go,
"Wow. Really blunt."

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.547
"Saturday Night Live" is --
season premiere is this weekend.

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:24.818
They're back, live, at 30 Rock.
-Yes.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.786
-Our buddy, Chris Rock,
is hosting.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:29.355
-Yeah.
Isn't that nice that they --

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:32.758
that Lorne was like, "You know
who'd be great for this time?

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:35.194
Old Chris Rock."
He -- He --

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:38.198
I was talking to Chris
a couple of weeks ago,

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.765
when he was thinking of hosting.

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:43.969
And I was very, like,
"There's nobody like you, buddy.

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:45.071
You have to do that."

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.672
He was excited.
And --

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.807
-Perfect.
-You know his monologue

00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:51.277
is gonna be incredible.
How about Rock,

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:54.446
anything he says,
even in conversation, you go,

00:01:54.446 --> 00:01:56.716
"There's no way
I would have thought of that,

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.085
ever, in my life,
but that's so on the money."

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.820
Everything he says
is so on the money,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.688
but you're just like, "Wow.

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:04.156
How did I not ever
think that way?

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:05.391
That's incredible."

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.093
-Well, you've known him
since stand-up, right?

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.461
Did you guys
do stand-up together?

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.729
-Yes, I knew Rock.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.432
We know each other
since 17 years old.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.433
Just like you.
You started real young, too.

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:17.003
I was just a young baby,
and I was kind of known

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.871
as the young guy in comedy.

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.973
And then,
I got to The Comic Strip,

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:23.075
and they kept -- Lucien,
who ran The Comic Strip...

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:24.944
-Yeah, Lucien Hold, yeah.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.113
-Lucien Hold kept saying,
"You and Chris Rock,"

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.581
and I kept saying,
"Who's Chris Rock?

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.717
What do you keep bringing this
other guy up to me?"

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.353
And they're like, "Well, he's
out with Eddie Murphy right now.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.687
Eddie Murphy loves him,"
and I was like,

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.589
"Eddie Murphy likes somebody,
not me?"

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.157
I was so upset.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.193
-And then --
And then, Rock came to the club

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:42.595
after hanging out with Eddie.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.430
And he came to the club,
and we met.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.899
And we just became
really tight immediately.

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:48.534
I was like,
"Oh, man, this guy is funny."

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.403
You know, I saw him --

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:53.806
I saw Rock like
10 years ago in Vegas.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:58.344
I went with Nicholson --
me, Nicholson, and Jim Brooks.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.680
-Wow.
-And I sat in between

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.915
Nicholson and Jim Brooks,
watching Rock,

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:05.518
and, literally, every time
I looked left or right,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.387
Nicholson was doubled over
and Jim Brooks was doubled over,

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:11.057
and I was going, "I wish Rock
could see this, man,"

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:14.526
'cause we were a few rows back,
and he was not getting to see --

00:03:14.526 --> 00:03:16.863
Imagine getting to see
Jack Nicholson and Jim Brooks

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.464
thinking you're the funniest guy
on the planet.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.533
Anyways, that was cool.
-Also, the thing I love

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.667
about Jack,
and you know this, too --

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.704
he laughs the way he talks,
kind of.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:27.907
Like, he goes like,
"Ha, ha ha, ha!

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:30.042
Ha ha!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:32.812
I'm like...
That's how he laughs.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.213
-Yeah.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:37.483
-I want to talk about
"Hubie Halloween."

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.351
-Yeah.
Why not, Jimmy?

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:41.154
-In a different --
to shift gears,

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:45.558
you dedicate the movie
to the late Cameron Boyce,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.860
who was supposed to be
in "Hubie Halloween,"

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.930
but he, sadly, passed away
before filming.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.332
-Yes, just a few days
before filming,

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:56.102
and that kid was a great kid.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.604
Just such a --
His family's amazing.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.006
I know him from "Grown-Ups."

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:02.708
He was a little kid
in "Grown-Ups,"

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:05.878
and I watched him grow up
and become, like, a superstar.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.947
My kids worshipped him.
Every ki--

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.783
He came to my daughter's
bat mitzvah.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.285
-Really?
-And he came

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:16.989
and literally signed -- I mean,
that bat mitzvah was gigantic.

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:20.727
There were like 400 people there
and massive amount of kids.

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.661
And he signed
every kid's autograph,

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:25.064
and everybody was freaking out
over Cameron.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.733
And he was just the nicest kid.

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:29.469
And he always
had charities going on

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:32.471
and always would speak to me
about, "Can you do this?

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:34.073
Can you do that?"
It was always for charity.

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.508
He didn't care
about anything else.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:39.578
And just a nice,
solid, talented kid.

00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:41.447
You know, like, when he was
a little kid --

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.849
Remember in "Grown-Ups,"

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:46.418
the "I want to get
chocolate wasted"?

00:04:46.418 --> 00:04:47.753
-Oh, yeah.
-It was like the --

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:51.390
the little girl said that,
Alexis says that.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.558
And -- And I think --

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:54.460
-"I want to get
chocolate wasted."

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.928
-Yeah.
She won, that year,

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.897
like, an MTV award,
Funniest Line or whatever,

00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:00.366
and she got the award.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:04.403
But Cameron said it around the
table when he was ad-libbing,

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:05.705
and everyone laughed.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:07.039
And then,
he said it a couple times,

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.775
and I go, "Cameron, you mind if
the little girl says it?

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:12.578
Might be funnier."
And he was like, "Okay."

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:13.679
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:16.416
And then --
And then, she did it.

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:18.117
Blah, blah, blah.
And then, after, I go,

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.852
"Cameron,
I can use yours or hers.

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.687
Whatever you want."
He goes, "Whatever --

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:25.158
Whatever's funniest, man," but
kind of like, "I'll kill you."

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.660
And then,
the next thing you know,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:31.264
the nice little girl gets --
And I saw Cameron years later.

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:33.366
I go, "That 'chocolate wasted,'
that's still bugging you."

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:35.935
He's like, "You owe me."
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.770
Oh, that's awesome.
That's cool.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:38.870
I didn't know
that he wrote that.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:41.440
That's cool.
"Hubie Halloween."

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:45.311
Is this your first
holiday film for Netflix?

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.445
-Yeah.
Yeah.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:48.047
They wanted to make
a holiday movie.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:51.250
I knew Chris--
if I made a Christmas movie,

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:55.220
people would say, "No, no, no.
I'm not buying that, buddy."

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.890
So I said, "Let's go Halloween.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.492
Let's go Halloween on you."

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.327
-So many funny people in this --
in this movie.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.595
I mean...
-Yes.

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:07.166
-So many funny people.
Tim Meadows, Maya Rudolph.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:10.669
-Yes.
Yeah, Kenan.

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:11.871
-Kenan's great.
Shaq is in it.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.539
Shaq's very funny.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:16.842
-Shaq's incredible.
Dan Patrick is in it!

00:06:16.842 --> 00:06:18.210
He yelled at me this morning!

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.379
He says I never mention
that he's in the movies.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:22.115
Dan Patrick.
-I'm sorry.

00:06:22.115 --> 00:06:23.816
We had to
edit that out for time, but...

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:26.752
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:26.752 --> 00:06:28.554
-That was good, Jimmy.

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:31.290
Dan is hilarious in it!
Thank you, Dan.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.593
-[ Laughing ]
I want to show a clip.

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:35.895
Here's Adam Sandler
in "Hubie Halloween."

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:37.497
Take a look.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:43.301
♪♪

00:06:43.301 --> 00:06:46.372
-[ Muffled shouting ]

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:48.440
-Michael Mundie.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:49.842
-[ Muffled shouting ]

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:54.713
-Listen, I am a fan of Halloween
zingers as much as the next guy,

00:06:54.713 --> 00:06:56.515
but --
-[ Muffled shouting ]

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:57.816
-What?
What are you saying?

00:06:57.816 --> 00:06:59.519
-[ Muffled shouting ]

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:03.589
-Michael?

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:04.590
Michael!

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.626
♪♪

00:07:07.626 --> 00:07:09.128
What d--

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:18.203
♪♪

00:07:18.203 --> 00:07:25.144
-[ Screaming ]

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:27.413
-Adam, thanks again
for coming on the show.

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:29.248
You're the best --
-Does it get better than that?

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:31.283
Does it get better
than that clip, Jimmy?

00:07:31.283 --> 00:07:32.718
-No.
-Oh. Right?

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:35.887
-The only way it can get better
is if it's a whole movie.

00:07:35.887 --> 00:07:37.489
-Yeah, that's it, man.

00:07:37.489 --> 00:07:39.758
-Adam Sandler, everybody.
"Hubie Halloween" premieres

00:07:39.758 --> 00:07:42.228
October 7th on Netflix.
Check it out.

